  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1258 PM CST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nPatchy fog is possible across the region this morning with skies\nclearing and winds going calm or light. We are already seeing \nsome lower visibilities across our sites and expect this to\ncontinue until at least sunrise.\n\nAnother mild day is in store today with mostly sunny skies and\nhighs in the mid to upper 60s as we await our next front.\nBeginning tonight and into Friday morning a positively tilted \ntrough will bring yet another cold front through the region. No\nrain is expected, but much colder air is. Highs are only\nforecast to reach the mid to upper 50s across most of the region\nwith portions of southern SE Missouri and southern west \nKentucky possibly reaching 60 degrees Friday afternoon. This\ncolder air will remain in place through the weekend with similar\nhighs expected. Furthermore, overnight lows will drop to the \nlow to mid 30s beginning Friday night and continuing through\nSunday night. With these temperatures a hard freeze is expected\nto end the growing season.\n\nDry conditions will persist for the next several days and into\nat least mid next week. High pressure will settle in Monday\nallowing for another warm-up into the low to mid 60s through the\nmiddle of next week.",
